**Critical performance rule:**

Employees performing different operations must be compared using standard-time-based productivity percentages, not raw production quantities.

For example:

- Head preparation: 2 minutes per unit.
- Body preparation: 4 minutes per unit.
- Hand preparation: 6 minutes per unit.
- Foot preparation: 3 minutes per unit.

Use the approved operation standards and existing Performance Calculation Engine.

Never compare 100 heads directly against 100 hands without considering operation standards and units of measurement.

